[Music]  a cartoon doesn't have to be funny in  order to be good  and i think that my work is is a  reflection of my sense of humor  but primarily i would consider myself  an artist who draws  his opinions about what is going on in  the news  in a way it's really no different than  what an editorial page  columnist would do but instead of using  a typewriter i'm using paper pen  and a drawing board  [Music]  you know a cartoon deals makes its point  through exaggeration  and exaggeration is certainly a large  part of caricature so when you're  drawing somebody  you're looking to accentuate or  exaggerate  certain features about that person to  make them very recognizable  you know hopefully getting to the point  after you  you've been drawing somebody for a while  where you don't need to use a label to  identify  that caricature so  in a way uh an artist can get away  with more than say a person who's  writing an opinion  but that's just the nature of caricature  and of satire  [Music]  bill clinton had a very has a very large  sense of humor  and he was one of the few presidents  that would actually  request uh original cartoons and he  enjoyed them and uh you know it was all  it was always a great charge to uh hear  from him  and have him uh request a cartoon it  took a while to learn  how to draw him uh which  you know my characters of him ended up  really concentrating on his chin  and exaggerating that chin in in order  to make him recognizable  and using his glasses a lot as a way to  make him recognizable  um so he was a fun and one of the  most fun cart presidents to caricature  i would say the same thing minus the  glasses  obviously there were a lot more cartoons  drawn about him because he was president  for two terms  but he was also a fun car uh fun  president to caricature  ronald reagan was probably one of the  best uh  presidents to caricature because he had  that  uh that pompadour in his hair he had a  lot of lines in his neck  and there you know it almost got to the  point where if you drew the hair  correctly you didn't really have to draw  too much else you could just make ronald  reagan  very recognizable a very difficult  president to caricature  there weren't a lot of things to  exaggerate  other than his ears and  he was probably one of the presidents  that was more  difficult to draw cartoons about  uh because my frankly a lot of my  politics align with his  so those eight years was a little more  difficult  to be as critical of him as some of the  other presidents that i've drawn  well the hair uh you know what can i say  uh  it's all about the hair and getting that  hair just right  and i think it took me at least three  years into his administration  to finally get to the point where i got  his hair to the point where  i actually liked the way it was drawn  and of course he was a treasure trove  for all  cartoonists because there was so much  controversy and so much constant news  about everything going on with him and  his administration  so he was a gold mine for cartoonists  [Music]  13 000 cartoons which is over a period  of uh over 35 years  uh these are all the cartoons that i've  drawn for the las vegas sun in my career  and these cartoons have been um you know  warehoused at the sun  and for the most part collecting dust  and we decided  that we needed to find um  a better way to preserve the cartoons  and to keep them  for any kind of future  research that students or classrooms  or individuals might be interested in  and unlv uh at their special collections  at the library special collections  department was very interested in taking  this  on and preserving the cartoons so we  were happy to  donate the work to them and they're  going to be able to  preserve it in a way that's accessible  to anybody that might want to  use it or read it or see it  it is often a lighthearted way  to make a point about what's going on in  the news there's a lot of  serious news going on and sometimes if  readers  can have a smile or a chuckle or  you know find some humor in something  that's going on in the news  i think that i think that makes them  feel good and makes them relate to the  cartoon

